---
layout: base.njk
title: Tax sale calendar
description: Upcoming county tax lien and tax deed sales by date, filterable by state, sale type and format.
permalink: /calendar/
---
<h1>Tax sale calendar</h1>
<p class="lede">Every dated sale we track, soonest first. Many counties also run sales on a fixed schedule; you'll find those on each county page.</p>
{% include "notice.njk" %}

<div class="filters" data-filter-table="#calendar">
  <select name="state" aria-label="State">
    <option value="">All states</option>
    {% for st in states %}<option value="{{ st.state }}">{{ st.name }}</option>{% endfor %}
  </select>
  <select name="type" aria-label="Sale type">
    <option value="">Liens and deeds</option>
    <option value="lien">Tax liens</option>
    <option value="deed">Tax deeds</option>
    <option value="redeemable deed">Redeemable deeds</option>
    <option value="hybrid">Hybrid</option>
  </select>
  <select name="format" aria-label="Format">
    <option value="">Online or in person</option>
    <option value="online">Online</option>
    <option value="in person">In person</option>
    <option value="both">Both</option>
  </select>
  <span class="muted" data-count></span>
</div>
<div id="calendar">
{% set rows = sales %}{% set showState = true %}
{% include "sales-table.njk" %}
</div>

<h2>Counties with a recurring schedule</h2>
<div class="table-scroll">
<table>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">County</th><th scope="col">Schedule as the county states it</th><th scope="col">Checked</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for c in counties %}{% if c.schedule_rule %}
    <tr><td><a href="{{ c.url }}">{{ c.county }}, {{ c.state.state }}</a></td><td>{{ c.schedule_rule }}</td><td class="nowrap">{{ c.lastChecked | shortDate }}</td></tr>
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

{% include "signup.njk" %}
